    "result_text": "The full test suite (the single `AcceptanceTest`, plus its base/helper classes) passes with **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the tenure-based membership rule in `Owner.getMembershipLevel()` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`):\n\n- The pre-tenure factors (base 1, +1 for email, +1 for `namesakeCount == 0`) are now capped at `MAX_MEMBERSHIP_LEVEL` (3) first.\n- Level 4 is then granted **only** when tenure \u2014 days elapsed since the owner's `registrationDate` \u2014 exceeds 365 days, computed with `ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(registrationDate, LocalDate.now())`.\n- I added a `MEMBERSHIP_TENURE_DAYS = 365` constant and the `java.time.temporal.ChronoUnit` import, and updated the Javadoc to describe the tenure-reserved level 4.\n\nBecause a newly created owner's `registrationDate` is today, its tenure is 0, so a new owner with an email and `namesakeCount` of 0 lands at level 3, never 4 \u2014 matching the specification and the acceptance test.",
