    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe tenure rule lives in exactly the right place: it's an additional factor in the already-existing `getMembershipLevel()` computation on the `Owner` model, appended after the pre-tenure cap rather than tangled into it. The `MEMBERSHIP_TENURE_DAYS` constant is placed right beside the related `MAX_MEMBERSHIP_LEVEL` constant and documented in the same style. Using `ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(...)` for a day count is idiomatic and consistent with the neighboring `getAgeBand()` method, which similarly inlines a `Period.between(...)` date computation against `registrationDate` \u2014 so inlining the tenure check here (rather than extracting a helper) matches the established convention of this class. No duplication, no catch-all growth, and the Javadoc was updated coherently to reflect the new behavior. A maintainer of this codebase would find it natural.",
